      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Cloud Vision API**\n\nI've decided to move forward with the Google Cloud Vision API for image label detection. Now, my focus is on integrating it within a `detect_image_labels.py` Python script. I want to make its use explicit and easily recognizable in the codebase.\n\n\n**Implementing the Detection Script**\n\nI'm now writing the Python code for `detect_image_labels.py`, focusing on clear integration with Google Cloud Vision. I'm importing the `google.cloud.vision` library and planning to initialize the client within the script. The goal is explicit identification of the Vision API as the image label provider. This will encompass all the necessary imports and client initialization.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861033903,
          "start": 1789861031567
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc07ee8f001Nwwbq7BBSgLMB0",
